Implemented exact daily replay labels, temporally censored multi-horizon features, cohort empirical-Bayes priors, character n-gram SVD, and a forward-CV-selected raw/log LightGBM plus ordered CatBoost ensemble.
Added measurement profile and critical-path time allocation without changing the immutable kapso_evaluation harness.
RepoMemory sections consulted: core.architecture, core.entrypoints, core.where_to_edit, core.invariants, core.testing, core.gotchas, core.dependencies
Recovered fast-evaluation failure: DuckDB 1.5.4 raised CatalogException for unsupported log1p; replaced SQL uses with ln(1+x).
Recovered second fast-evaluation failure: feature derivation dropped the timestamp join key with intermediate datetime columns, causing KeyError: 'timestamp'; preserved timestamp and bumped the cache content version.
Suppressed pandas fragmentation warnings, applied native LightGBM categorical handling, added normalized-title ordered CatBoost encoding, and corrected separate raw/log selected iteration counts.
Added strictly availability-aware replay-label encodings for ad, normalized title, category, and category-region-price groups, plus ordered CatBoost AdID encoding; each row uses only origins whose four-day label window has ended.
Rejected and reverted replay-label/AdID encodings after all three forward heads degraded: selected blend mean MAE rose from 0.03142927 to 0.03165779 and worst-fold MAE from 0.03408131 to 0.03445908. The post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted because the internal gate had already rejected the block.
Forward-fold leaf selection chose 31 leaves over 47/63 for both LightGBM heads, favoring the simpler tied design. Added recent-versus-previous cohort trends for SearchStream, VisitStream, and PhoneRequestsStream plus six-hour burstiness features for a new forward-fold feature gate.
Rejected and reverted the widened 502-column recent-cohort/burstiness block: mean forward MAE was 0.03145761 versus 0.03142927 for the simpler 406-column matrix, with only a 0.00003681 worst-fold improvement; the difference was far inside one standard error, so the simpler feature block won the prescribed tie break. The post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted after consuming the gate result.
Staged the already-cached intfloat/multilingual-e5-small model after securing the core score, using it only on static ad titles, offline, with PCA fit on the model-A-safe title corpus. The general pretrained model supplies no Avito event or label history, so it cannot leak either prediction window.
Rejected and reverted the 32-dimensional multilingual-E5 title block: forward mean MAE was 0.03149387 and worst-fold MAE 0.03425835, both worse than the character-SVD core at 0.03142927/0.03408131. Cached raw embeddings remain registered for later independent reuse; the post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted.
Added a mild 0.97-per-day replay-origin recency weight for an internal temporal-shift gate, following the campaign memory's independently measured stable setting.
Rejected and reverted 0.97 daily recency weighting for this ensemble: mean/worst forward MAE were 0.03139932/0.03416125 versus 0.03138635/0.03412092 unweighted. The tied simpler unweighted design won, and the post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted.
Added a compact, four-day-delayed target-history gate containing only prior ad last/median/count and category/category-region-price median fallbacks, separating it from the rejected wide target-encoding block.
Rejected and reverted the compact target-history block as well: mean/worst forward MAE were 0.03143176/0.03417739 versus 0.03138635/0.03412092 without it. The post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted.
Raw-head feature-block screening selected a compact moment representation: removing 72 redundant raw sums/counts while keeping their means, dispersions, extrema, and shares changed mean MAE from 0.03147161 to 0.03146182 and improved worst-fold MAE from 0.03420094 to 0.03403964.
The common compact block hurt log-L1 and CatBoost, so feature routing now uses the 319-field compact representation only for raw-L1 while retaining all 391 selected fields for log-L1 and CatBoost.
Added a query-semantics feature gate from SearchInfo: temporal 4-day/all query length and token moments, unique query counts, and normalized query-in-title match share.
Rejected and reverted query-semantics widening: mean/worst forward MAE degraded to 0.03142311/0.03416865 from 0.03136740/0.03400884 for query presence plus context alone. The post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted.
Added an internal gate for explicit category×price-band and category×audience-region categorical keys, complementing their historical cohort priors.
Rejected and reverted explicit crossed categorical keys: mean/worst forward MAE degraded sharply to 0.03160923/0.03436892 from 0.03136740/0.03400884. The post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted.
CatBoost categorical screening removed the high-cardinality normalized-title key while retaining character SVD and title EB features: CatBoost mean/worst MAE improved from 0.03183940/0.03437613 to 0.03169936/0.03424224.
CatBoost text-block screening then removed the 24 character-SVD coordinates from that head while retaining title shape and EB priors: CatBoost mean/worst MAE improved further to 0.03156655/0.03407467. Raw/log LightGBM retain character SVD as the reliable text baseline.
Rejected a second CatBoost seed after averaging it inside the fixed blend worsened mean/worst forward MAE from 0.03131447/0.03393563 to 0.03132758/0.03394051.
Added an internal gate for compact conditional-denominator proxies: projected four-day exposure from 1/2/4/8-day histories and one-, two-, and three-click ratios, including conservative blended and trend projections.
Rejected and reverted the 24 simple denominator proxies: mean/worst forward MAE degraded to 0.03145591/0.03415677 from 0.03136740/0.03400884 for the head-routed core. The post-fold final fit was intentionally interrupted.
